quick_facts: Discovered by Ernest Rutherford (1911, gold-foil experiment)
quick_facts: Diameter ~100,000 times smaller than the atom itself
quick_facts: Holds over 99.9% of the atom's mass
quick_facts: Protons and neutrons bound by the strong nuclear force
